# Git commits and pull requests

**Default (happy-housing):** After every completed task, validate (`make check` + quality/perf/correctness review), then **commit and push**. Message format and granularity below still apply. Do not ask for permission to commit/push task work — `AGENTS.md` requires it.

**Pull requests:** Still propose title and body; create only when the user asks.

## Commits

Prefer **granular** commits — one logical change per commit. Split when changes span unrelated concerns (e.g. MLflow tracking vs report vs CI).

If a single commit would bundle too much, **split into multiple commits** (still push after the task completes).

### Message format

Short **type** prefix + brief summary. Optional body with bullet details when helpful.

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `test`, `refactor`, `chore`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`

- Subject: imperative, lowercase type, no period, ~72 chars
- Body: what changed and why — not a file list unless useful
- One concern per commit; do not mix unrelated types

### Before committing

1. Run `make check` (and any task-specific correctness checks)
2. Run `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -5` (parallel)
3. Draft message(s) matching the split plan
4. Stage only files for that commit; commit; verify with `git status`
5. `git push` (set upstream with `-u` when needed)

Do not `--no-verify`, amend, or force-push unless user rules explicitly allow.

## Pull requests

Propose title and body; create only when asked.

**Body:**

```markdown
## Summary
- Bullet: user-facing or architectural outcome

## Test plan
- [ ] make check
- [ ] …
```

Keep PRs focused. Use `gh pr create` with HEREDOC body when user approves.
